{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448899-damage-location","id":1448899,"title":"Damage location","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-18T14:32:48-07:00","id":1448899,"title":"Damage location","content":"Hello guys, i was wondering: how do you manage the damage depending on where the player hit? i'm asking because some fight maneuver are targeting legs or little places of the body (like the crotch). In this case do you limit the damages? <br /> If the garou hit the foot of a giant fomori, or the legs it seems strange to just apply the damage and kill the creature like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T15:53:08-07:00","id":1448906,"title":"","content":"Garou are magical war-machines with supernaturally potent claws and fangs.... so generally I don't worry too much about it. Most things the Garou fight either have a close-ish to human anatomy, including major blood vessels all over the place to sever, or are made of spirit-stuff and it doesn't really matter where you hurt them anyway.<br /> <br /> The system also has a few things here:<br /> <br /> 1) Targeted attacks have a higher difficulty, reducing average damage. Clawing at a leg to maim it is less likely to result in a fatal blow than just attacking.<br /> <br /> 2) A bunch of combat maneuvers like sweeps and kicks don't do damage or default to bashing damage, making if very hard to kill someone. If a Garou kicks you in the crotch, they can hit hard enough to break your hip and KO you, but outright killing would be rare, because they're dealing bashing damage. <br /> <br /> 3) Super sized foes tend to have lots of health and/or lots of soak, which means they're hard to take out by just nibbling on their legs. You're probably looking at something that resembles drawing and quartering as a pack of Garou sink into different limbs and rip them off in a group effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T06:23:18-07:00","id":1448974,"title":"","content":"Lots of health? I knew spirit use their essence as life point when it come to combat but according to the book, when we're not in the umbra the health is the same as physical being, 8 level including death.<br /> A fomori power make them 3 times bigger but there's no indication of more health :/<br /> Of course it's possible to create a specific fomori with lot of soak when they're transformed, plus their gifts to get stronger: like one whit bone armor and a gifts or 2 to get even more resistant and force the players to target specifics parts of it's body","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 05-19-2021, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:14:31-07:00","id":1449001,"title":"","content":"The size altering fomori power in W20 core literally gives +1 HL per instance.<br /> <br /> And I completely missed the for some reason W20 cut the line in the Materialize Charm that says to give Materialized spirits more health for larger forms, but that was always how the previous editions did it.<br /> <br /> Plus there are things like thunderwyrms and skull pigs that have more than standard health as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T12:10:52-07:00","id":1449025,"title":"","content":"A was also asking that because the level 4 metis gift of porcupine, if the attacker don't have enough stamina or success on his soaking roll he could be incapacitated by a simple claws attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T12:26:05-07:00","id":1449026,"title":"","content":"I'm.... not really sure what the connection is. Yes, a baddie that has high damage output that hits someone using Gift of the Porcupine can incap or even kill themselves from it. But that would also be a lot of damage for the Gift user as well. What does that have to with hit locations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T13:15:25-07:00","id":1449040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448899-damage-location?p=1449001#post1449001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The size altering fomori power in W20 core literally gives +1 HL per instance.<br /> <br /> And I completely missed the for some reason W20 cut the line in the Materialize Charm that says to give Materialized spirits more health for larger forms, but that was always how the previous editions did it.<br /> <br /> Plus there are things like thunderwyrms and skull pigs that have more than standard health as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised gave spirits extra HLs if they were meant to just be bigger, but editions prior to that required payment in Power to create a material form meant that they paid to have health levels and were bigger if they had more than seven, a reversed cause and effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T17:31:15-07:00","id":1449063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448899-damage-location?p=1449026#post1449026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm.... not really sure what the connection is. Yes, a baddie that has high damage output that hits someone using Gift of the Porcupine can incap or even kill themselves from it. But that would also be a lot of damage for the Gift user as well. What does that have to with hit locations?</div> </div> </div> </div>The connection is that if the player face a garou using the gift of porcupine and giving him a punch or a claws attack, the only part of his body damage if he has less than 5 success is a part of his arm or his hand with a direct punch, but if his strength is at 9 in crinos form and he don't have enough stamina or soaking success the player could be incapacitated or really badly injured by an injury that does not affect a vital part of his body, then wouldnt'it be better to ajust the damage and apply an handicap to the player? Like his arm is in to bad condition to be used until he healed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 05-19-2021, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T18:09:09-07:00","id":1449065,"title":"","content":"You are aware that a common way of attempting suicide involves the blood flow to the hand, right? You can bleed to death from a serious laceration to your hand.<br /> <br /> Punching someone covered in six inch long magical <b>barbed</b> spikes is a wonderful way to shred every blood vessel in your hand, wrist, and upper arm, which can kill you very quickly. <br /> <br /> On top of this porcupine quills are even worse than just being sharp. Their barbs don't just stick in, every muscle movement causes them to keep digging in deeper. Animals that tangle with porcupines frequently die, just not immediately: infection, lose of function of limbs making it hard to catch food, barbs that block the throat, barbs work deeper in an damage arteries or organs, etc. This is just going faster... with a very high level Gift not having quills.<br /> <br /> Plus anything in WtA is dealing with the reality of it being used on things with Rage, that can bounce back from fatal damage, and some pretty potent low level healing powers.<br /> <br /> You're making a huge deal out of, &quot;...he don't have enough stamina or soaking success the player could be incapacitated...&quot; which is true, but the math of the system doesn't support it being likely.<br /> <br /> Lets say our character has Strength 9/Stamina 8 in Crinos (that's 5 in each in Homid).<br /> <br /> There is only a ~6.45% chance of doing 7+ damage in the first place. So the vast majority of the time, they aren't going to be doing enough damage to take themselves out in one hit.<br /> <br /> There's a ~65.72% chance of soaking enough of the damage that no matter how much damage it does, the werewolf isn't taking enough damage to go to incapacitated.<br /> <br /> A fully healthy Garou attacking someone using that Gift and killing themselves on it is such a vanishingly rare event, that something like, &quot;The quills slice through the attacking arm, and then shred it as the force of Crinos muscles pull them free and sprays blood everywhere. After what seems like gallons of blood geysers over both, the attacker falls over from the blood loss, reverting to their breed form.&quot; Might sound rare and extreme, but that's exactly what the rolls would be, so it fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T23:46:42-07:00","id":1449094,"title":"","content":"I'm mastering my first story as GM, so i'm not used to all system and narration 'x) and i'm counting too much on the Book rule to the point that i didn't even think about the blood loss. I know that i might be asking stupid questions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}